{
    "name": "E2E GitLab MCP - List Tools",
    "description": "Spawns the bundled server.js: ListTools returns all 9 tools. CallTool is not covered: the E2E account holds a placeholder token, and the server reports API errors as JSON-RPC errors (as the original package did), so a call fails the component.",
    "notes": {
        "197aec08-7be8-4840-aabd-c6774b75c4ed": {
            "x": 64, "y": 160, "width": 672, "height": 192,
            "content": "## Test data assumption\n\nThe E2E account `E2E GitLab MCP (placeholder token)` holds an invalid token (GITLAB_API_URL `https://gitlab.com/api/v4`), so this flow only proves that the engine installs the connector and spawns `server.js` over stdio.\n\nTo cover CallTool, put a real GitLab PAT in the account and add CallTool `search_repositories` with `search: appmixer`. With the placeholder token the call fails with `MCP error -32603: GitLab API error: Unauthorized`."
        }
    },
